		<guid isPermaLink="false">https://stereogum.com/?p=2505329</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[<p>Theoretically, Nick Hakim makes soul music, but it’s more like visiting spirit music. The Queens-based polymath, a trusted collaborator for figures as disparate as Adrianne Lenker and Lil Yachty, can be heard on many kinds of records. But he may be doing his finest work in his own catalog, crafting spectral R&#38;B songs with sound design so immaculate it becomes an instrument unto itself.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://stereogum.com/2505329/album-of-the-week-nick-hakim-i-can-see/reviews/album-of-the-week/">Album Of The Week: Nick Hakim &lt;em&gt;I Can See&lt;/em&gt;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://stereogum.com">Stereogum</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
		
		
