					<description><![CDATA[<p>We need to bring back compilations. I mean, we won't. You can understand why we won't. Compilations are fully technologically obsolete, since streaming services turn everything into compilations. You no longer need to buy the soundtrack album for some movie that you'll never watch to hear 15 bands that you like and/or tolerate and/or are curious to check out and/or have never heard of. Also, compilations must be an almighty pain in the ass to coordinate. But when a compilation hits right, that's a glorious feeling. When you walk into a record store and you're like, "Wait, <em>they're</em> on it? And <em>her</em>? And these other two people, <em>together</em>?" And then you take it home and all the songs from disparate artists somehow work as a single listening experience? That's the stuff, baby.</p>
<p>The post <a href="https://stereogum.com/2490550/album-of-the-week-war-childs-help2/reviews/album-of-the-week/">Album Of The Week: Various Artists&#8217; &lt;em&gt;HELP(2)&lt;/em&gt;</a> appeared first on <a href="https://stereogum.com">Stereogum</a>.</p>
]]></description>
		
		
		
